Description: Let thumbnail plugins take precedence over standard thumbnailers
 The plugins are loaded before the standard thumbnailers so that they take
 precedence, but the wildcards of a group (video/*) were looked up after every
 exact MIME type, standard thumbnailers included (BUG 453480). So a standard
 thumbnailer that names video/mp4, such as the one of ffmpegthumbnailer, made
 the thumbnails of MP4 files even with ffmpegthumbs enabled, and kept what
 ffmpegthumbs adds, such as both views of a stereo video, out of them. A MIME
 type is now looked up among the plugins first, by its name, its parents and
 its group, and only then among the standard thumbnailers.
Author: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: no
